Finding: {"title":"qb_entity_map has no DB-level unique constraint despite comments claiming one; insert() has a check-then-act race","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"business-rules / concurrency","files":["src/lib/schema/quickbooks.ts","src/repositories/quickbooks/qbEntityMapRepo.ts"],"detail":"`src/lib/schema/quickbooks.ts` line 91 comments the `atosEntityIdx` as \"Critical: composite unique enforces one mapping per ATOS entity per school\", but it is defined via `index(...)` (lines 92-96), not `.unique()` — Drizzle's `index()` builder produces a plain non-unique btree index. There is no DB constraint preventing two rows with the same `(flightSchoolId, atosEntityId, atosEntityType)`. `qbEntityMapRepo.insert()` (src/repositories/quickbooks/qbEntityMapRepo.ts:126-165) does a `SELECT` (`findLegacy`) to check for an existing row and only inserts if none is found — a check-then-act race with no transaction/advisory lock.","impact":"Two concurrent sync attempts for the same ATOS entity (e.g. a webhook-triggered CDC sync racing a manual admin sync) can both pass the `findLegacy` check before either inserts, producing duplicate `qb_entity_map` rows for the same entity. Downstream lookups use `.limit(1)` with no ordering, so which mapping 'wins' is nondeterministic — potential double-posting to QuickBooks or SyncToken confusion (stale-token write failures, per the file's own doc comment on line 69).","recommendation":"Add a real unique index (Drizzle `uniqueIndex`) on `(flight_school_id, atos_entity_id, atos_entity_type)` and use `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`/`DO UPDATE` in `insert()` instead of check-then-insert, mirroring the idempotent pattern already used correctly in `qbWebhookEventRepo.insertIfNew`.","confidence":"MEDIUM"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.
